.TH "CSSROTATE" "3JS" "September 29, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSRotate \- CSSRotate
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSRotate\f[B]\f[R] interface of the CSS Typed Object
Model API represents the value of a rotation function in the
\f[CR]transform\f[R] property in CSS.
.SH CONSTRUCTOR
.TP
\f[B]CSSRotate()\f[R]
Creates a new \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R] object.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
\f[I]Also inherits properties from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSTransformComponent\f[I].\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]angle\f[R]
Represents the angle of rotation.
.TP
\f[B]x\f[R]
Represents the x\-coordinate of the rotation axis vector.
.TP
\f[B]y\f[R]
Represents the y\-coordinate of the rotation axis vector.
.TP
\f[B]z\f[R]
Represents the z\-coordinate of the rotation axis vector.
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
\f[I]Also inherits methods from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSTransformComponent\f[I].\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSRotate\f[B]\f[R] interface is used to represent
rotation functions in a list of \f[CR]transform\-function\f[R]s defined
for a CSS \f[CR]transform\f[R] property.
This includes rotations declared with: \f[CR]rotate()\f[R],
\f[CR]rotate3d()\f[R], \f[CR]rotateX()\f[R], \f[CR]rotateY()\f[R], or
\f[CR]rotateZ()\f[R].
.PP
The list itself is represented by a \f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R] object
that can be iterated to get the objects representing each of the
functions (and may include objects representing other transforms).
.PP
A rotation is defined by an axis vector (\f[CR]x\f[R], \f[CR]y\f[R],
\f[CR]z\f[R]) and an \f[CR]angle\f[R] of rotation around that axis.
The 2\-argument constructor form is shorthand for a rotation around the
z\-axis: it sets the axis to \f[CR](0, 0, 1)\f[R], which is why a 2D CSS
\f[CR]rotate()\f[R] is equivalent to
\f[CR]rotate3d(0, 0, 1, angle)\f[R].
The 4\-argument form lets you specify any axis, for an arbitrary 3D
rotation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
This example constructs a \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R] and logs its structure
and properties.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] rotate = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSRotate(CSS.deg(45));

console.log(rotate); \f[I]// CSSRotate {x: CSSUnitValue, y: CSSUnitValue, z: CSSUnitValue, angle: CSSUnitValue, is2D: true}\f[R]
console.log(rotate.angle.value, rotate.angle.unit); \f[I]// 45 \(dqdeg\(dq\f[R]
console.log(rotate.x.value, rotate.y.value, rotate.z.value); \f[I]// 0 0 1\f[R]
console.log(rotate.toString()); \f[I]// \(dqrotate(45deg)\(dq\f[R]
.EE
.SS Incrementing a rotation
This example demonstrates how \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R] might be used.
.PP
Note that there is hidden logging code that isn\(cqt relevant to the
example.
.SS HTML
First we define the elements for the box to rotate, and the button we
use to rotate it.
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]div\f[R] id=\(dqincrement\-box\(dq></\f[B]div\f[R]>
<\f[B]button\f[R] id=\(dqincrement\-button\(dq>Rotate 15°</\f[B]button\f[R]>
.EE
.SS CSS
The CSS for the box we will rotate is shown below.
Note that the box is initially rotated by 15 degrees.
.IP
.EX
increment\-box {
  \f[B]width\f[R]: 100px;
  \f[B]height\f[R]: 100px;
  \f[B]margin\-bottom\f[R]: 1rem;
  \f[B]background\-color\f[R]: #6666dd;
  \f[B]transform\f[R]: rotate(15deg);
  \f[B]transition\f[R]: transform 0.3s ease;
}
.EE
.SS JavaScript
The code first gets a handle to the box we\(cqre rotating, then uses
\f[CR]computedStyleMap()\f[R] to get and log the initial transform
angle.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] incrementBox = document.getElementById(\(dqincrement\-box\(dq);

\f[B]let\f[R] angle = incrementBox.computedStyleMap().get(\(dqtransform\(dq)[0].angle.value;
log(\(gainitial angle: ${angle}deg\(ga);
.EE
.PP
Then we get the button and add a handler to rotate it 15 degrees each
time the button is clicked.
Note that we use \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R] to define the rotation, add it to
a \f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R], and then set that as the style for the
box.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] incrementButton = document.getElementById(\(dqincrement\-button\(dq);
incrementButton.addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  angle = (angle + 15) % 360;
  \f[B]const\f[R] rotate = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSRotate(CSS.deg(angle));

  incrementBox.attributeStyleMap.set(
    \(dqtransform\(dq,
    \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTransformValue([rotate]),
  );
  log(\(gaangle: ${angle}deg\(ga);
});
.EE
.SS Result
This example starts with a box already rotated \f[CR]15deg\f[R] in CSS.
Click the button to rotate it.
